# Vendored crate sources are committed verbatim — cargo verifies every file
# against .cargo-checksum.json, so a single dropped file breaks the build on a
# fresh clone (this is exactly what the repo's top-level `target/` rule did to
# the `cc` crate's `src/target/` module). Override every inherited ignore so
# the vendor tree is always complete; `cargo vendor` produces a clean tree, so
# there is nothing here we don't want tracked.
!*

# …but never let local-only junk slip into the vendored tree. `!*` above
# re-enables every inherited ignore (incl. the repo's), so re-ignore the
# usual editor/OS artifacts here. No published crate ships these names, so
# this can't drop a real vendored source file.
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
*~
